A lifted free type parameter whose origin name ("server") equals another set’s
name exercises the lifted-parameter namer (ReservedNames / freshLiftedName)
rather than the local allocator. Use is an anchor (its type parameter appears only
in its input), so "server" is lifted onto set build’s header and x becomes an
input; the "server" set emits a func named "server". On regeneration the
re-scanned output file must not reserve "server" for the lifted-parameter namer,
so re-running plumb over its own output reproduces it byte-for-byte.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
output: plumb_gen.go
-- example.com/app/app.go --
package app

type Thing struct{}

//plumb:build
func Use[server any](x server) *Thing { return &Thing{} }

//plumb:server
func NewServer() *int { return nil }
